The '''2018 United States House of Representatives elections''' will be held on November 6, 2018. Elections will be held to elect representatives from all 435 [[List of United States congressional districts|congressional districts]] across each of the 50 [[U.S. state]]s. [[Delegate (United States Congress)|Non-voting delegates]] from the [[District of Columbia]] and four of the five inhabited [[Insular area|U.S. territories]]{{efn|Not including the [[Resident Commissioner of Puerto Rico]], who serves a four-year term.}} will also be elected. The [[United States House of Representatives election in the Northern Mariana Islands, 2018|election for non-voting delegate]] from the [[Northern Mariana Islands]] has been postponed until Tuesday, November 13, 2018, due to the impact of [[Typhoon Yutu]].<ref name=hsa>{{cite news|first=Jennifer |last=Sinco Kelleher |title=Northern Mariana Islands elections delayed as community recovers from devastating super typhoon |url=http://www.staradvertiser.com/2018/10/29/breaking-news/northern-mariana-islands-elections-delayed-as-community-recovers-from-devastating-super-typhoon-yutu/ |work=[[Associated Press]] |publisher=[[Honolulu Star-Advertiser]] |date=2018-10-29 |accessdate=2018-11-03 |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20181030015123/http://www.staradvertiser.com/2018/10/29/breaking-news/northern-mariana-islands-elections-delayed-as-community-recovers-from-devastating-super-typhoon-yutu/ |archivedate=2018-10-30 |deadurl=no}}</ref>

The winners of this election will serve in the [[116th United States Congress]], with seats apportioned among the states based on the [[2010 United States Census]]. [[Republican Party (United States)|Republicans]] have held a House majority since January 2011 (see [[United States House of Representatives elections, 2010|2010 results]]), although they lost five seats in the 2016 elections and [[Pennsylvania's 18th congressional district special election, 2018|another]] in special elections leading up to the 2018 election.

The [[United States midterm election|midterm elections]] will take place halfway through Republican President Donald Trump's term. The [[United States Senate elections, 2018|2018 Senate elections]], [[United States gubernatorial elections, 2018|2018 gubernatorial elections]], and many [[United States elections, 2018|state and local elections]] will also be held on this date.

