=== Non-retirements ===
Some members announced their retirements, but either rejoined the race or resigned early and were replaced in a special election. Sorted by district name.
# {{ushr|CO|7|X}}: [[Ed Perlmutter]] (D) announced his retirement April 9, 2017, to [[Colorado gubernatorial election, 2018|run for Governor of Colorado]]. He returned to the House race on August 21, 2017.
# {{ushr|NY|27|X}}: [[Chris Collins (American politician)|Chris Collins]] (R): Renominated but then withdrew after being indicted for [[insider trading]].<ref>{{cite news | date=August 11, 2018 | title=Rep. Chris Collins (R-N.Y.) suspending reelection bid after being charged with insider trading | url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/politics/wp/2018/08/11/rep-chris-collins-r-n-y-suspending-reelection-bid-after-being-charged-with-insider-trading/?noredirect=on&utm_term=.7d3a333218c5 | work=[[Washington Post]] | access-date=August 11, 2018 }}</ref> On September 17, 2018, he got back in the race.<ref>https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/17/nyregion/chris-collins-congress-election-campaign.html</ref>
# {{ushr|PA|7|X}}: [[Pat Meehan]] (R) announced his retirement January 25, 2018.<ref>{{cite news | last=Tamari | first=Jonathan | date=January 25, 2018 | title=Rep. Pat Meehan will not seek reelection after sexual harassment furor | url=http://www.philly.com/philly/news/politics/rep-pat-meehan-will-not-seek-reelection-after-sexual-harassment-furor-20180125.html | work=[[The Philadelphia Inquirer]] | location=Philadelphia, PA | access-date=January 25, 2018 }}</ref> He resigned April 27, 2018 and his seat will be filled by a [[#Special elections|special election, see below]].
# {{ushr|PA|15|X}}: [[Charlie Dent]] (R) announced his retirement September 7, 2017.<ref name="Debonis">{{cite web | last1=DeBonis | first1=Mike | title=Rep. Charlie Dent, outspoken GOP moderate, will not seek reelection | url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/powerpost/wp/2017/09/07/rep-charlie-dent-outspoken-gop-moderate-will-not-seek-reelection | website=Washington Post | accessdate=September 7, 2017}}</ref> He resigned May 12, 2018,<ref name=abcApril172018>{{cite web | url=http://abc6onyourside.com/news/nation-world/gop-congressman-charlie-dent-resigning | title=GOP Congressman Charlie Dent resigning | first=ERIN VOGEL-FOX, | last=Circa | accessdate=May 22, 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.rollcall.com/news/politics/gop-rep-charlie-dent-resigning-coming-weeks | title=GOP Rep. Charlie Dent Resigning 'In the Coming Weeks'}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.politicspa.com/dent-announces-saturday-exit-from-congress/87456 | title=Dent Announces Saturday Exit From Congress | accessdate=May 22, 2018}}</ref> and his seat will be filled by a [[#Special elections|special election, see below]].
# {{ushr|TX|27|X}}: [[Blake Farenthold]] (R) announced his retirement December 14, 2017. He resigned April 6, 2018, and his seat was filled by a [[#Special elections|special election, see below]].
# {{ushr|UT|3|X}}: [[Jason Chaffetz]] (R) announced his retirement April 19, 2017. He resigned June 30, 2017, his seat was filled by [[#Special elections|special election, see below]], and the winner is running for re-election in November 2018.

